Machine Learning vs. Data Science

Machine Learning System: 
"Field of study that gives compuers he ability to learn without being explicitly programmed"
  Input A (Sq Ft of house, # bath, # room, newly renovated(Y/N))
  Input B (Price of house based on variables in Input A)
  This is an A to B mapping Machine Learning System 
ML learning often results in a running AI system (websites/mobile app)
  This is a piece of software that can run Inputs A and create result Input B, 24/7
  ML is often software that computes data based on pre-exisiting variables and trends. 

A team might analyze a data set of house variable and find that: 
"The science of extracting knowledge and insights from data"
  "Homes with 3 bedrooms are more expensive than homes with 2 bedrooms of a similar size"
This is an ex. of data science projects. 
Analysts use data to make descions/predictions. 
  The output is usually a slide deck/presentation that summarizes the findings from the 
  data to implement improvements. 

Deep Learning 
Input: Size, # of bed, # of bath, newly Renovated(Y/N)
Feed this into a (Artificial) Neural Network which finds the estimated price of a house based on Input.
  This a mathematical equation that computes B based on Inputs A. 

AI has many tools
  Machine learning/data science
  Deep learning/neural networks
  Generative AI
  unsupervised learning, reinforcement learning
  graphical models, planning, knowledge graph, etc. 

AI is a huge set of tools for making computers behave intelligently 
  The biggest subset are tools from ML
    Inside ML the part that is recently importatnt is Deep learning and Neural Networks. 
  AI has other smaller tools that are growing and are important
    Gen AI, Unsupervised and reinforcement learning, graphical models, planning,   
    knowledge graph, etc. 
Data Science is a intersecting study that uses ML, Deep learning, and other AI tools in combination with Data Science Specific tools. 
